profile: ext_setext_headings=on
# Setext headings

Setting: `ext_setext_headings`. On in the Markdown-like profile.

A paragraph followed by a line of `=` is a level 1 heading.

``` example
A heading
=========
```

A line of two or more `-` makes a level 2 heading.

``` example
A heading
--
```

A single `-` is a list marker and does not underline.

``` example
A paragraph
-
```

The underline applies to the paragraph above it, so the heading can span
several lines.

``` example
A heading
on two lines
===
```

Without a paragraph above, the same line is what djot reads.

``` example
===
```

## What it costs

A paragraph can no longer be wrapped anywhere: a line that is all `=`, or
two or more `-`, ends the paragraph and changes what it is.

